        <body>
            <div xml:id="d210">

                <pb facs="0410" n="1370" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1370"/>

                <head>No. 923.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Buck.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-08-14"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 14,
                        1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 224.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your No. 48 of the 30th of
                    October, 1885, I transmit for your files a copy of a letter of Mr. S. N. Pettis
                    touching the alleged outrage on V. H. MacCord, an American citizen, to which
                    your dispatch refers.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d210-a1.xml" xpointer="d210-a1"/>
